variables: * - tutorial: The tutorial definition. * - images_path: Path to the
tutorial images. */ #} {% set header_content %}
<p>
  The IBM API Connect Developer Portal allows you to customize the front page of
  your site to better align with your brand and help users quickly discover your
  APIs.
</p>

<p>
  In this tutorial, we'll walk through creating custom blocks, arranging them on
  a page, and setting that page as your new front page. This approach avoids
  inline styling and relies on your theme for rendering, making it easier to
  update the design later without changing content stored in the database.
</p>

<p>This tutorial covers the following steps:</p>
<ul>
  <li>Creating custom content blocks</li>
  <li>Creating and configuring a page</li>
  <li>Adding the custom blocks to the page</li>
  <li>Changing the site front page</li>
</ul>

<p>This is how the current front page looks like</p>
<img
  src="{{ images_path }}/current-frontpage.png"
  alt="Current Front Page"
  class="img-responsive"
  loading="lazy"
/>
{% endset %} {% set steps_content %}
<li class="gs-step" data-step="Create Custom Blocks">
  <h3>Creating Custom Blocks</h3>
  <p>1. Navigate to:</p>
  <div class="path-instruction">
    <strong>Content → Blocks → Add content</strong>
  </div>
  <p>
    2. Enter <strong>Block 1</strong> in the <strong>Block description</strong>.
  </p>
  <p>
    3. In the body area, click <strong>Source</strong> and paste the following
    HTML:
  </p>

  <div class="command-block">
    <pre><code class="language-html">&lt;div class=&quot;tutorial_block_1 tutorial_block_frontpage&quot;&gt;
      &lt;h1&gt;&lt;span&gt;Create with our APIs&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
      &lt;p&gt;&lt;span&gt;Welcome to our Developer Portal where you will find APIs to create your awesome app.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
      &lt;/div&gt;</code>
    </pre>
  </div>

  <img
    src="{{ images_path }}/block-creation.png"
    alt="Create a Content Block"
    class="img-responsive"
    loading="lazy"
  />

  <p>4. Click <strong>Save</strong>.</p>
  <div class="success-message">
    <p>You’ve successfully created Block 1!</p>
  </div>

