<li class="gs-step" data-step="Create and Configure a Page">
  <h3>Creating and Configuring a Page</h3>
  <p>1. Navigate to:</p>
  <div class="path-instruction">
    <strong>Structure → Pages → Add page</strong>
  </div>

  <img
    src="{{ images_path }}/pages-list.png"
    alt="Pages List"
    class="img-responsive"
    loading="lazy"
  />

  <p>
    2. Enter <code>Portal home</code> in the
    <strong>Administrative title</strong> field.
  </p>
  <p>3. Enter <code>/newhome</code> in the <strong>Path</strong> field.</p>
  <p>
    4. For <strong>Variant type</strong>, select <code>Panels</code> and click
    <strong>Next</strong>.
  </p>
  <img
    src="{{ images_path }}/page-information.png"
    alt="Pages List"
    class="img-responsive"
    loading="lazy"
  />
  <p>
    5. Accept the defaults for <strong>Labels</strong> and select
    <strong>Standard</strong> for <strong>Builder</strong>, then click
    <strong>Next</strong>.
  </p>
  <p>
    6. From <strong>Layout</strong>, select
    <strong>Two column bricks</strong> under Bootstrap and click
    <strong>Next</strong>.
  </p>
  <p>7. Adjust classes as follows:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Top Left</strong>: Small:9</li>
    <li><strong>Top Right</strong>: Small:3</li>
    <li><strong>Bottom Left</strong>: Small:4</li>
    <li><strong>Bottom Right</strong>: Small:8</li>
  </ul>

  <img
    src="{{ images_path }}/page-layout.png"
    alt="Two Column Bricks Layout"
    class="img-responsive"
    loading="lazy"
  />
</li>

<li class="gs-step" data-step="Add Custom Blocks to Page">
  <h3>Adding the Custom Blocks to the Page</h3>
  <p>
    1. Leave the <strong>Page title</strong> blank and click
    <strong>Add new block</strong>.
  </p>
  <p>
    2. Under <strong>Content block</strong>, select <strong>Block 1</strong>.
  </p>

  <img
    src="{{ images_path }}/add-block.png"
    alt="Adding Block to Page"
    class="img-responsive"
    loading="lazy"
  />

  <p>
    3. Clear the <strong>Display title</strong> checkbox, select
    <strong>Top Left</strong> as the region, then click
    <strong>Add block</strong>.
  </p>
  <p>4. Repeat the process to add:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Block 2</strong> → Top Right</li>
    <li><strong>Block 3</strong> → Bottom Left</li>
    <li><strong>Block 4</strong> → Bottom Right</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    5. Click <strong>Finish</strong> and then <strong>Update and save</strong>.
  </p>

  <div class="success-message">
    <p>All blocks are now placed on your custom page!</p>
  </div>
</li>

<li class="gs-step" data-step="Change Front Page">
  <h3>Changing the Front Page</h3>
  <p>
    <strong>Note:</strong> The original front page remains available as a backup
    in case you need to revert.
  </p>
  <p>
    1. Navigate to your new page at <code>/newhome</code> to confirm it looks
    correct.
  </p>
  <p>2. Then go to:</p>
  <div class="path-instruction">
    <strong>Configuration → System → Basic site settings</strong>
  </div>
  <p>
    3. In the <strong>Default front page</strong> field, enter
    <code>/newhome</code>.
  </p>
  <p>4. Click <strong>Save configuration</strong>.</p>

  <img
    src="{{ images_path }}/updated-frontpage.png"
    alt="Updated Front Page"
    class="img-responsive"
    loading="lazy"
  />

  <div class="success-message">
    <p>
      Congratulations! Your new custom page is now the front page of your
      Developer Portal.
    </p>
  </div>
</li>
